.TH QIMGVR 1 "2026-10-21" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qimgvr \- view images and video with optional stereoscopic XR output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
qimgvr [OPTIONS] [PATH]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The default CMake build uses the patched FLTK 1.4.5 frontend with OpenGL,
OpenCV, Exiv2 and embedded libmpv. It provides browsing, thumbnails, image
editing and save, metadata, slideshow and video playback. Still-image depth
conversion runs in a separate Arc SBS worker; ordinary viewing does not need
that worker or its model. Existing packed SBS can bypass depth inference.
.PP
The retained Qt frontend is a separate build, explicitly selected with
.BR \-DDE_XR_TOOLKIT=Qt6 .
Its shortcuts, settings and extra CLI options differ from the FLTK defaults.
.SH FLTK OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-sbs[=auto|always|off]
Select stereo output. Default auto; the bare option selects always.
The modes may also be supplied as a separate argument.
Always uses XR output when available or a local SBS preview otherwise.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sbs
Disable stereo output.
.TP
.BI "\-\-input\-layout=" auto|2d|full\-sbs|half\-sbs
Override input packing. Default auto. A separate argument is also accepted.
.TP
.B \-\-build\-options
Print compiled frontend features without opening a window.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print build identity without opening a window.
.TP
.BI "\-\-smoke\-test " OUTPUT.png
Render a diagnostic capture and exit. This argument is a filename, not a duration.
.PP
FLTK does not currently implement a CLI help page or thumbnail-generation CLI.
Normal DomeD launches need no explicit routing option; presenter transport
arguments are internal worker details.
.SH FLTK CONTROLS
Ctrl+O opens a file; Ctrl+Shift+S saves as; Ctrl+Z undoes edits.
Left/Right browse, F fits, 1 shows actual pixels, T toggles thumbnails,
and F11 toggles fullscreen. E/Q rotate, H/V flip, and C crops a selection.
S selects Stereo / Always (XR or preview); the Stereo menu also selects
Off, Auto and the input packing override.
.PP
For video, Space plays or pauses, Alt+Left/Right seek, M mutes,
and plus/minus changes volume. Native command menus are exported through
DBusMenu/KDE AppMenu where the session supports them.
.SH XR AND APPEARANCE
DomeD owns its XR Wayland socket, input seat and headset session; the viewer
uses verified stereo surfaces without starting another OpenXR session there.
The patched FLTK frontend follows DomeD palette and bitmap-font changes live.
The Arc worker, prepared model and runtime/GPU support must be installed separately.
Physical headset, WiVRn streaming and hardware inference behavior require
validation on the target system.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QIMGV_SBS_PYTHON
Worker Python containing arc_sbs and dependencies. FLTK uses
/opt/arc-sbs/venv/bin/python when present, otherwise python3.
.TP
.B QIMGVR_SBS_DEVICE, QIMGVR_SBS_RENDERER
Optional worker device and renderer overrides.
.TP
.B LD_LIBRARY_PATH
Must resolve the matching patched FLTK 1.4.5 runtime when it is privately installed.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Selects the configuration root, normally ~/.config.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/qimgvr/fltk.json
FLTK settings, separate from Qt qimgv configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dome/appearance.json
Live DomeD appearance settings.
.SH QT FRONTEND
The opt-in Qt build additionally implements its original thumbnail-generation
options, Qt image plugins and settings under ~/.config/qimgv.
F8 toggles its SBS output and F9 changes its input override.
These are not FLTK shortcuts. Full RAW, animation, ICC, printing and high-quality
resampling parity remain incomplete in FLTK.
.SH INSTALLATION
Use an optimized CMake build and stage it as the regular user before system
installation. The FLTK target installs its executable only; stage this manual
and desktop/MIME integration separately. The legacy install-local.py helper
assumes Qt features but does not currently pass the explicit Qt CMake selector.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR arc\-sbs (1),
.BR mpvr (1),
.BR dome\-compositor (1)
